#: processes/sdlc/requirements-filing.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Determine whether this filing promotes a proposal from docs/proposals/<slug>.md (promote), amends an existing requirement or replaces it with a new requirement (amend-or-supersede), or retires an obsolete requirement (retire). Assign the primary semantic concern group from code-lists/concern-group.json (sdlc, process, tools, kg, library, content, ui, conduct) and verify that req:<slug> does not collide across docs/proposals/ and docs/requirements/."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/requirements-filing.bpmn:28
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Executes the deterministic filing steps under methodologies/requirements-filing-and-organisation.md: classifies the filing mode and concern group, promotes the proposal via git mv (preserving git blame and proposedIn), binds Requirement front matter and three-axis lineage, updates superseded or retired records in place, updates docs/requirements/index.md, runs check:requirements, and records the human sign-off attestation."
msgstr ""

