#: processes/sdlc/requirements-filing.bpmn:18
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Proposed filing process for bean folio-assistant-qh1s (issue #1164): how a proposal in docs/proposals/<slug>.md is promoted into docs/requirements/<slug>.md when its feature ships, or how an existing filed requirement is amended in place, superseded by a new requirement (status: superseded + supersededBy: req:<new-slug>), or retired (status: retired) without deleting historical records. Every filed requirement keeps its flat path docs/requirements/<slug>.md (id: req:<slug>) and is organised in docs/requirements/index.md under its canonical concern group from code-lists/concern-group.json, verified by check:requirements, and signed off by the Business Analyst / Owner."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/requirements-filing.bpmn:113
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record requirement-signoff attestation and set stage"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/requirements-filing.bpmn:62
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Record the last commit SHA touching docs/proposals/<slug>.md, execute `git mv docs/proposals/<slug>.md docs/requirements/<slug>.md` so git log --follow preserves the proposal's history, and record `proposedIn: { commit, path: \"docs/proposals/<slug>.md\" }` in the YAML front matter."
msgstr ""

